From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:04:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 069/138] drm: adp: t7000: Put the panel to sleep when the CRTC
 is turned off

Turning the CRTC off (DPMS off or ACTIVE=0) only stopped the vblank
interrupt; the panel kept refreshing behind a zero backlight.

With the new panel_sleep parameter (default off, writable at runtime),
CRTC off also sends the panel what ApplePinotLCD sends first on display
off: DCS display off, then enter sleep mode, through the Synopsys DSI
host's generic packet interface (0x6c header, 0x74 status, the same
registers iOS and adp-mipi.c use). CRTC on sends exit sleep mode and
display on, 120 ms apart, but only if this driver put the panel to
sleep. The DSI link, the timing generator and the pipe keep running, so
no panel or DSI re-init is involved.

Also complete a flip still waiting for its vblank when the CRTC goes
off, add a debugfs "panel" file to test sleep/wake without DRM master,
and always leave the panel awake on remove and shutdown.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/adp/adp-t7000.c | 182 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 181 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

